0..77 Comment "// A `hold` or a `fork` in a match arm whose ends continue the block. Another"
78..155 Comment "// arm exits early, so each local end of the match runs the rest of the block"
156..232 Comment "// itself, inside whatever scope its arm opened: the arm\'s held slot, or the"
233..312 Comment "// fork\'s parent end. The rest still reads the slots it named before the match,"
313..344 Comment "// past the one the arm opened."
